WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.330
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.600 --> 00:07.590
[6:30 A.M. Alarm]

3
00:13.910 --> 00:15.590
Yikes!

4
00:16.950 --> 00:19.910
Hajime Suzuki, high school sophomore.

5
00:19.910 --> 00:21.880
Okay.

6
00:21.880 --> 00:25.290
I like to write stories and daydream.

7
00:28.640 --> 00:31.410
My genre of choice is BL.

8
00:32.760 --> 00:34.480
Until a while ago,

9
00:34.480 --> 00:38.570
enjoying BL was just a hobby of mine.

10
00:38.570 --> 00:40.080
Perfect.

11
00:40.080 --> 00:41.730
But now...

12
00:45.020 --> 00:46.560
Good morning.

13
00:46.560 --> 00:49.500
Morning, Suzupi!

14
00:54.670 --> 00:56.230
Morning, Suzuki.

15
00:56.230 --> 00:58.120
Don't scare me like that.

16
00:58.120 --> 01:00.500
Good morning, Serizawa.

17
01:02.910 --> 01:06.640
Now, I have a real crush on a boy.

18
01:06.640 --> 01:08.390
How's the novel coming along?

19
01:08.390 --> 01:10.680
- Made any good progress? - Yeah.

20
01:10.680 --> 01:12.440
It's almost done.

21
01:12.440 --> 01:13.770
Seriously?

22
01:13.770 --> 01:14.980
Nice work.

23
01:14.980 --> 01:16.560
Haruto Serizawa.

24
01:16.560 --> 01:18.850
- Morning, Serizawa. - Morning.

25
01:18.850 --> 01:21.020
His presence is dazzling,

26
01:21.020 --> 01:23.640
and he's full of warmth.

27
01:23.640 --> 01:25.810
He's like our sun.

28
01:26.550 --> 01:32.080
Of course, I know my crush is unrequited.

29
01:33.720 --> 01:35.680
Still...

30
01:36.580 --> 01:39.810
[Fin]

31
01:41.440 --> 01:44.810
I did it.

32
01:44.810 --> 01:46.620
It's done.

33
01:47.410 --> 01:49.420
I have to text Serizawa.

34
01:53.410 --> 01:57.100
No, I'll tell him in person.

35
01:58.420 --> 02:03.270
Even if I can never tell him how I feel...

36
02:06.210 --> 02:09.160
I miss him.

37
02:12.300 --> 02:15.170
I love Serizawa.

38
02:59.410 --> 03:02.560
[Episode 10]

39
03:02.560 --> 03:04.100
Okay.

40
03:04.100 --> 03:06.270
- Go! - Serizawa?

41
03:07.080 --> 03:08.630
Huh?

42
03:09.300 --> 03:10.950
Morning.

43
03:11.830 --> 03:14.290
- Goal! - Where's Serizawa?

44
03:14.290 --> 03:18.030
[Morning. Are you coming to school today?] [I need to tell you something...]

45
03:20.760 --> 03:22.090
Suzuki.

46
03:22.090 --> 03:24.670
You've been staring at your phone all day.

47
03:24.670 --> 03:27.620
Are you that lonely without Serizawa around?

48
03:29.340 --> 03:32.240
Yeah. I am.

49
03:32.950 --> 03:35.080
You really do miss him.

50
03:36.140 --> 03:37.790
Actually,

51
03:37.790 --> 03:41.990
I finished writing my novel yesterday.

52
03:41.990 --> 03:45.120
The one you're always writing during lunch?

53
03:45.120 --> 03:47.030
- Yeah. - For real?

54
03:47.030 --> 03:49.150
That's awesome! Congrats!

55
03:49.150 --> 03:51.600
- Thanks. - I realize we never asked,

56
03:51.600 --> 03:53.990
but what's your novel about?

57
03:53.990 --> 03:55.840
Oh yeah, good question.

58
03:55.840 --> 03:58.190
Well...

59
03:59.930 --> 04:04.280
The protagonist is a loner,

60
04:04.280 --> 04:06.910
who has no confidence in himself.

61
04:08.160 --> 04:12.520
But one day, he becomes friends with the popular guy in school.

62
04:13.690 --> 04:15.590
Eventually, they fall in love.

63
04:17.110 --> 04:20.620
And then they chase their dreams together.

64
04:20.620 --> 04:22.860
That's the general synopsis.

65
04:24.110 --> 04:28.940
I see. So, that's what you were writing about.

66
04:28.940 --> 04:31.350
Are we allowed to read it?

67
04:31.350 --> 04:32.850
Yeah, can we?

68
04:32.850 --> 04:34.630
- You really want to? - Of course.

69
04:34.630 --> 04:35.800
- Right? - Yeah.

70
04:35.800 --> 04:37.540
- I'd also want to read your work. - Same.

71
04:37.540 --> 04:38.710
Sure, go ahead.

72
04:38.710 --> 04:40.270
Awesome!

73
04:40.270 --> 04:41.530
Time to get reading.

74
04:41.530 --> 04:44.750
Let's see here...

75
04:44.750 --> 04:46.780
I changed my mind.

76
04:48.040 --> 04:49.620
Sorry.

77
04:49.620 --> 04:53.460
I want Serizawa to read it first.

78
04:54.380 --> 04:57.040
Can you guys wait until after he finishes?

79
05:00.470 --> 05:02.720
Why are you all grinning?

80
05:02.720 --> 05:03.850
No reason.

81
05:03.850 --> 05:06.860
We were just wondering why Serizawa?

82
05:06.860 --> 05:10.310
That's because Serizawa

83
05:10.310 --> 05:15.210
is my first reader.

84
05:15.210 --> 05:17.190
Your first reader.

85
05:18.610 --> 05:20.720
Is that really it?

86
05:25.530 --> 05:27.810
- Guess it can't be helped. - Yeah.

87
05:27.810 --> 05:28.880
Then I'll be reader two.

88
05:28.880 --> 05:31.590
I'll be reader three.

89
05:38.200 --> 05:40.570
He still hasn't replied.

90
05:43.510 --> 05:46.940
Suzuki! What's up?

91
05:47.830 --> 05:49.290
I have the surveys from the festival.

92
05:49.290 --> 05:51.800
Hey, thanks a million.

93
05:51.800 --> 05:53.400
Speaking of the festival,

94
05:53.400 --> 05:57.230
could you put these pictures up in the classroom somewhere?

95
05:57.230 --> 05:59.530
Sure thing.

96
05:59.530 --> 06:02.700
The festival sure was a blast, huh?

97
06:02.700 --> 06:06.680
We owe it all to your efforts, Suzuki.

98
06:08.420 --> 06:14.360
You must have been worried when I volunteered for the committee.

99
06:14.360 --> 06:15.480
Huh?

100
06:15.480 --> 06:19.090
I'm a gloomy introvert.

101
06:19.090 --> 06:23.790
And I'm not exactly "festival committee" material.

102
06:23.790 --> 06:26.470
I must have seemed unreliable at the time.

103
06:27.300 --> 06:30.320
If only I could be a bit more like Serizawa.

104
06:32.130 --> 06:34.100
Is that what you think?

105
06:34.100 --> 06:37.820
Well, I thought you fit the role, and you were super dependable.

106
06:39.350 --> 06:44.240
All that introvert-extrovert business,

107
06:44.240 --> 06:47.000
and stuff about MBTI types?

108
06:47.000 --> 06:51.800
That's just people wanting to categorize themselves.

109
06:53.060 --> 06:57.490
But human beings aren't as simple as that.

110
07:00.100 --> 07:05.180
Everyone's got a different side to them.

111
07:05.180 --> 07:08.710
Secrets they can't tell their friends.

112
07:08.710 --> 07:10.100
It'll be fine.

113
07:10.100 --> 07:13.010
Worries they only share with their lover.

114
07:13.010 --> 07:14.720
It's okay.

115
07:14.720 --> 07:17.640
Look, Usamin's proposal is going viral!

116
07:17.640 --> 07:21.130
For real? Oh my god!

117
07:23.080 --> 07:27.140
Anxieties they keep to themselves.

118
07:29.800 --> 07:31.710
Does it bother you?

119
07:33.720 --> 07:36.140
Don't poke at my wounds.

120
07:42.870 --> 07:45.200
So, here's the thing, Suzuki.

121
07:45.200 --> 07:48.920
There's no need to categorize yourself like that.

122
07:50.450 --> 07:52.580
Besides...

123
07:52.580 --> 07:54.950
Personally, I think Serizawa's a real weirdo

124
07:54.950 --> 07:58.780
especially when you're involved.

125
07:59.840 --> 08:02.260
Me?

126
08:08.400 --> 08:10.680
Excuse me.

127
08:11.960 --> 08:13.580
Hello, Serizawa?

128
08:13.580 --> 08:15.330
Are you okay?

129
08:15.330 --> 08:18.140
- Huh? - I just saw your text.

130
08:18.140 --> 08:21.280
You said you had something to tell me.

131
08:21.280 --> 08:22.590
Is everything okay?

132
08:22.590 --> 08:24.660
Is this good news? Bad news?

133
08:24.660 --> 08:27.660
Serizawa, calm down.

134
08:27.660 --> 08:29.100
Where are you?

135
08:29.100 --> 08:31.820
Me? I just got to school, and...

136
08:34.910 --> 08:37.130
Suzuki!

137
08:37.130 --> 08:39.300
Are you seriously okay?

138
08:39.300 --> 08:41.030
You aren't hurt or anything?

139
08:41.030 --> 08:44.050
No, I'm perfectly fine.

140
08:45.050 --> 08:46.950
Thank god.

141
08:46.950 --> 08:49.110
You had me sweating bullets.

142
08:49.110 --> 08:51.550
Serizawa.

143
08:51.550 --> 08:53.230
I did it.

144
08:54.370 --> 08:57.190
I finished writing my novel.

145
08:57.190 --> 08:59.250
For real?

146
08:59.250 --> 09:00.810
That's awesome!

147
09:00.810 --> 09:02.820
Great job, Suzuki!

148
09:02.820 --> 09:07.160
I wanted to have you read it.

149
09:07.160 --> 09:08.930
Would you?

150
09:08.930 --> 09:10.290
Of course.

151
09:10.290 --> 09:11.590
Come on, let's go.

152
09:11.590 --> 09:13.150
- Right now? - Now.

153
09:13.150 --> 09:14.390
But class is in session.

154
09:14.390 --> 09:16.040
Don't care.

155
09:16.040 --> 09:17.870
I want to read it, now.

156
09:32.630 --> 09:34.760
I finished.

157
09:34.760 --> 09:37.640
How was it?

158
09:37.640 --> 09:40.250
Can I be honest with you?

159
09:41.470 --> 09:43.000
Go ahead.

160
09:43.890 --> 09:47.610
I feel like I'm going to cry.

161
09:47.610 --> 09:48.650
Huh?

162
09:48.650 --> 09:51.560
The characters got their happy ending.

163
09:51.560 --> 09:55.210
It's really a happily ever after.

164
09:55.210 --> 09:59.140
I'm so emotional.

165
10:02.100 --> 10:04.540
- Really? - Really.

166
10:04.540 --> 10:06.690
The whole story made my heart race.

167
10:06.690 --> 10:09.550
And then when I remember you wrote it,

168
10:09.550 --> 10:13.140
my heart gets so overwhelmed.

169
10:22.630 --> 10:24.570
What about you?

170
10:26.410 --> 10:29.750
How do you feel?

171
10:32.380 --> 10:35.870
I...

172
10:37.660 --> 10:39.920
I feel so happy, too.

173
10:43.330 --> 10:46.300
I've always hated myself

174
10:46.300 --> 10:49.690
for never finishing any of my works.

175
10:49.690 --> 10:51.710
I couldn't forgive myself.

176
10:53.130 --> 10:56.070
It was a cycle of frustration and failure.

177
11:01.660 --> 11:04.850
So, I'm happy I managed to finish a story.

178
11:06.120 --> 11:09.190
And I'm glad you get to read it, too.

179
11:12.160 --> 11:17.650
Honestly, I still can't believe it.

180
11:22.180 --> 11:25.140
You're reading something I wrote.

181
11:25.140 --> 11:27.410
You, the person I look up to.

182
11:28.540 --> 11:31.090
My...

183
11:31.090 --> 11:33.360
No, our sun.

184
11:35.900 --> 11:38.370
Someone who I assumed

185
11:38.370 --> 11:41.950
I'd never cross paths with.

186
11:43.440 --> 11:45.410
And yet...

187
11:47.110 --> 11:51.250
You continued to stay by my side.

188
11:53.170 --> 11:55.460
You've read my novel...

189
11:58.260 --> 12:00.980
And you really seem to enjoy it.

190
12:04.930 --> 12:06.660
I can't.

191
12:08.640 --> 12:10.600
I...

192
12:11.370 --> 12:15.230
I'm so happy.

193
12:16.310 --> 12:19.030
I'm seriously so happy.

194
12:20.420 --> 12:23.770
You're right here.

195
12:25.320 --> 12:31.510
Right at my side.

196
12:32.920 --> 12:35.130
Nothing could make me happier than that.

197
12:46.230 --> 12:48.510
Me too.

198
12:48.510 --> 12:52.830
I'm also happy to be here.

199
13:12.200 --> 13:13.800
What's up?

200
13:14.720 --> 13:16.630
It's nothing, but...

201
13:16.630 --> 13:18.880
Is it just me or...

202
13:18.880 --> 13:24.060
do you smell like...

203
13:24.060 --> 13:27.170
Soy sauce?

204
13:28.070 --> 13:30.240
You noticed?

205
13:30.240 --> 13:34.020
I actually had something to show you, too.

206
13:42.680 --> 13:44.770
Ta-da!

207
13:45.640 --> 13:49.040
I made this stew just earlier.

208
13:49.040 --> 13:50.220
What?

209
13:50.220 --> 13:53.640
Huh? You don't remember?

210
13:53.640 --> 13:55.740
But we made a promise.

211
13:58.140 --> 14:02.900
In the meantime, I'll work hard on becoming the King of Stewing.

212
14:04.150 --> 14:07.180
You mean...

213
14:07.180 --> 14:11.590
Yeah. Since you said you were almost done writing,

214
14:11.590 --> 14:14.020
I realized I needed to catch up.

215
14:14.020 --> 14:16.040
So...

216
14:16.040 --> 14:18.690
Does that mean...

217
14:20.800 --> 14:22.610
you've become...

218
14:22.610 --> 14:24.680
The King of Stewing!

219
14:26.000 --> 14:28.480
Why are you laughing?

220
14:28.480 --> 14:30.520
Because...

221
14:30.520 --> 14:32.470
The King of Stewing!

222
15:07.260 --> 15:08.960
Sorry!

223
15:09.740 --> 15:11.370
I'll head back first.

224
15:11.370 --> 15:12.930
Okay.

225
15:22.010 --> 15:23.150
All right. [Banana Lake]

226
15:23.150 --> 15:27.250
I now call this meeting to order.

227
15:27.250 --> 15:28.670
Pleased to have you all.

228
15:28.670 --> 15:31.000
Likewise.

229
15:34.170 --> 15:36.560
So...

230
15:36.560 --> 15:38.280
What's the issue today?

231
15:38.280 --> 15:41.070
Serizawa and Suzuki almost kissed.

232
15:41.070 --> 15:42.650
Again?

233
15:42.650 --> 15:45.070
And this time it's only "almost"?

234
15:45.070 --> 15:46.280
Meeting adjourned.

235
15:46.280 --> 15:48.090
- Yeah. - Call it off.

236
15:48.090 --> 15:51.290
- No more of this. - Yep.

237
15:52.860 --> 15:55.140
And they're not gonna stop us.

238
15:56.510 --> 15:59.230
- Back up, back up. - Why?

239
15:59.230 --> 16:01.180
What's the deal, really?

240
16:01.180 --> 16:03.220
Serizawa.

241
16:05.270 --> 16:06.900
I'm sorry.

242
16:08.300 --> 16:12.650
I lied to you.

243
16:12.650 --> 16:14.100
Huh?

244
16:15.420 --> 16:19.480
When we were at the beach,

245
16:19.480 --> 16:23.150
you asked me if I had a crush on anyone.

246
16:23.150 --> 16:26.890
At the time, I said no.

247
16:28.510 --> 16:30.420
But I was lying.

248
16:35.490 --> 16:38.270
To tell you the truth...

249
16:40.080 --> 16:42.590
since then, I...

250
16:44.300 --> 16:46.750
Serizawa, I...

251
16:50.530 --> 16:52.400
I've liked you.

252
16:56.310 --> 16:59.720
Of course, I know you have a crush,

253
16:59.720 --> 17:01.980
who also isn't me.

254
17:01.980 --> 17:03.320
- Huh? - So, really...

255
17:03.320 --> 17:05.320
You can just flat out reject me.

256
17:05.320 --> 17:06.740
Wait, hold on.

257
17:06.740 --> 17:08.130
Huh?

258
17:09.780 --> 17:15.340
The person I have a crush on is you.

259
17:16.910 --> 17:18.970
What are you talking about?

260
17:30.150 --> 17:32.370
Sorry.

261
17:32.370 --> 17:34.760
I'm not following.

262
17:34.760 --> 17:36.720
What are we talking about?

263
17:36.720 --> 17:40.850
We're talking about how Serizawa likes you.

264
17:40.850 --> 17:43.350
Yeah.

265
17:43.350 --> 17:46.400
You seriously never noticed?

266
17:46.400 --> 17:49.280
Hold on.

267
17:49.280 --> 17:52.370
But Serizawa got into BL in freshmen year because of his crush.

268
17:52.370 --> 17:55.100
Yeah, he did.

269
17:55.100 --> 17:58.460
His crush.

270
17:58.460 --> 17:59.820
That can't be.

271
17:59.820 --> 18:03.390
I only met Serizawa this year.

272
18:03.390 --> 18:07.350
And by then, he already liked BL.

273
18:08.940 --> 18:10.810
Oh, I see now.

274
18:11.970 --> 18:13.070
Huh?

275
18:13.070 --> 18:15.020
I'll explain.

276
18:15.020 --> 18:18.310
Come on, let's go.

277
18:18.310 --> 18:20.400
Where?

278
18:20.400 --> 18:22.610
Isn't that obvious?

279
18:22.610 --> 18:25.230
Somewhere we can be alone.

280
18:29.300 --> 18:32.380
Go get 'em!

281
18:33.350 --> 18:35.800
Thank you.

282
18:35.800 --> 18:37.960
- I say a toast is in order. - Agreed.

283
18:37.960 --> 18:40.670
Cheers!

284
18:43.260 --> 18:45.460
Hold on a second.

285
18:45.460 --> 18:47.720
Let me get this straight.

286
18:48.670 --> 18:54.270
So, you saw me reading BL in freshmen year,

287
18:54.270 --> 18:57.040
and that got you into it, too?

288
18:57.040 --> 18:58.490
Yeah.

289
18:59.150 --> 19:00.500
That doesn't add up.

290
19:00.500 --> 19:03.780
Then that means I'm your crush.

291
19:03.780 --> 19:05.610
You are.

292
19:05.610 --> 19:08.510
Haven't I made that clear already?

293
19:08.510 --> 19:11.110
I like you.

294
19:11.110 --> 19:14.690
You're my one and only.

295
19:14.690 --> 19:16.410
Got it?

296
19:17.690 --> 19:19.680
No, I don't get it.

297
19:19.680 --> 19:23.560
You're everyone's sun.

298
19:23.560 --> 19:25.470
Don't wanna be.

299
19:42.700 --> 19:46.700
Make me exclusively yours.

300
19:52.190 --> 19:53.980
You...

301
19:55.730 --> 19:58.700
You really...

302
19:58.700 --> 20:00.590
like me?

303
20:02.580 --> 20:04.420
Yeah.

304
20:04.420 --> 20:06.060
I do.

305
20:08.020 --> 20:09.940
What about you?

306
20:11.300 --> 20:15.200
Do you like me, too?

307
20:17.750 --> 20:19.210
Yeah.

308
20:20.640 --> 20:22.350
I do.

309
20:23.760 --> 20:25.540
Awesome.

310
20:25.540 --> 20:28.030
I'd repeat this conversation any day.

311
20:29.770 --> 20:33.230
Suzuki, I like you, too.

312
20:34.390 --> 20:38.960
Will you accept my feelings for you?

313
20:43.650 --> 20:46.540
Cute! Good boy.

314
20:46.540 --> 20:48.660
My Suzuki.

315
20:49.770 --> 20:52.030
Wait! I'm still confused!

316
20:52.030 --> 20:56.110
You, liking me? That has to be a mistake.

317
20:56.110 --> 20:58.540
My head feels like it's going to explode...

318
21:06.720 --> 21:09.790
Okay. Then how about this?

319
21:09.790 --> 21:14.150
Let's keep going, until it's hammered into your head.

320
21:15.250 --> 21:16.640
Huh?

321
21:16.640 --> 21:20.790
That's why I wanted us to be alone.

322
22:14.320 --> 22:16.560
So?

323
22:16.560 --> 22:18.450
Get it now?

324
22:23.920 --> 22:28.040
Not yet.

325
22:30.130 --> 22:32.470
Could you...

326
22:33.820 --> 22:35.650
try again?

327
22:37.610 --> 22:39.560
Suzuki.

328
22:40.740 --> 22:42.600
You're adorable.

329
22:45.840 --> 22:47.550
Okay.

330
22:48.880 --> 22:52.220
Then once more.

331
23:01.260 --> 23:04.980
Today's the day I make Serizawa flustered.

332
23:04.980 --> 23:07.390
So, this is what you like, Suzuki?

333
23:07.390 --> 23:10.010
Thanks for the meal.

334
23:10.010 --> 23:12.420
I keep getting flustered!

335
23:12.420 --> 23:14.800
Me!
